# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for tonight's four-card window (scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it):
# copy it over .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of tp4/serve-3 and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN.
# Nothing here names a rig, a card, a host or a registry: the cards are resolved at run time. Every value is final.
# ORDER.txt says the order, each job's image, its stop rule and its minutes. The image is tp4-serve-3 throughout: T1 builds it, the
# later jobs serve it, and a commit after T1's tag needs a new tag and every later job the new one.
# T5n (fallback, conditional): T5 with the graph part of the census off, c2-packed-tp4-diag-nograph (QWEN_FAST_TRACE_CENSUS_GRAPH=0).
# Run it ONLY if T5 was refused at attach, or its packed capture failed, with a ttnn.graph / '[PINDIAG] trace census unavailable' line
# in the log: the graph capture around a trace capture has never run on this stack, and the profiles are baked into the image, so this
# twin is the fallback without a new commit. The watchdog, the stage markers, the collectives log and the L1 view stay; the freed
# temporaries and '[PINDIAG] trace overlap' lines do not. Otherwise the same tests and the same reading as T5. Skip it if T5 booted.
# Duration (estimate): 20 min. Not a stop job.
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=reset smoke
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-serve-3
C2_PROFILE=c2-packed-tp4-diag-nograph
C2_SMOKE_TESTS=warmup,coding,long_real_text,concurrent4_v164order,concurrent4_steady,replay_concurrent4
